ioquake3 for RISC OS
====================

Quake III Arena's engine (ioquake3), for RISC OS 5 on a Raspberry Pi 2 or
later (best on a Pi 4). The 3D is drawn by the processor, with riscos-mesa's
OpenGL, so it runs at a low resolution scaled up to fill the screen.

Game data
---------
ioquake3 is the engine only. Put game data beside !RunImage, in this
application:

 - The free Quake III Arena demo: put demoq3.pak0/pk3 from the demo
   (linuxq3ademo-1.11-6.x86.gz.sh, or any copy of the demo) in the
   demoq3 folder. demoq3.zz-ioq3-vm/pk3, already there, holds
   ioquake3's game code, which the demo's own is too old for.
 - The full game: make a baseq3 folder and put pak0/pk3 to pak8/pk3 in
   it (pak1 to pak8 are the free 1.32 point release).
 - OpenArena (free, openarena.ws): put the pk3 files from OpenArena
   0.8.8's baseoa folder in a baseoa folder here. It's slower than
   Quake III (its maps draw more): about 12 to 20 frames a second.

!Run uses baseq3 if it's there, else baseoa, else demoq3.

You need SharedUnixLibrary and ARMEABISupport (from PackMan). For sound,
SharedSoundBuffer and StreamManager, or DigitalRenderer, in !System.

Playing
-------
Double-click !ioquake3. It starts full screen at the desktop's
resolution, drawing 300 lines (on a Pi 4 about 25 to 35 frames a second
with bots) and scaled up by the Pi's display hardware (VideoOverlay).
The mouse turns; the keys are Quake's (Setup > Controls to change them).

Settings that matter for speed (in the console, or q3config.cfg):

  r_renderHeight 300   lines drawn (240 is faster, 360 sharper;
                       0 draws at the full screen size: very slow)
  r_renderWidth 0      0: as wide as the screen's shape needs
  r_overlay 1          scale with the display hardware (VideoOverlay)
  r_vertexLight 1      one pass per surface: about 4 times as fast as
                       lightmaps on riscos-mesa
  r_fastsky 1          a plain sky: about 12% faster
  r_textureMode GL_NEAREST_MIPMAP_NEAREST
                       blockier textures: about 18% faster
  r_glFastest 1        keeps mipmapped textures on riscos-mesa's fast
                       path (3 times as fast as 0)
  r_ext_multitexture 0 two passes instead of two texture units, which
                       riscos-mesa does slowly (OpenArena: twice as fast)

Each of these needs vid_restart (or a restart) to take effect.

Windowed: r_fullscreen 0, r_mode -1, r_customwidth/r_customheight.

Files
-----
The console log, settings and screenshots go in the game's folder
(demoq3, baseoa or baseq3). stdout and stderr are in this application.

Source and licence
------------------
ioquake3 is GPL 2 (or later): the source, with the RISC OS changes, is
at the project's home. It uses riscos-mesa (Mesa, SDL2, OpenAL Soft:
MIT/zlib/LGPL) and UnixLib. Quake III Arena's data is id Software's and
isn't included.
